Package: budgetsc
Type: Package
Title: Reproducible Synthetic-Control and Bayesian Post-Estimation Pipeline for the Household Budgeting Study
Version: 0.4.6
Authors@R: person("Andre", "Bonfrer", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "andre.bonfrer@deakin.edu.au")
Description: Analysis pipeline for the digital-budgeting and financial-wellbeing
    project. A run is described by a specification (spec) with a deterministic
    identifier; runs read a single processed analysis panel, fit regularised
    multi-outcome synthetic controls (augMultiSynth), estimate heterogeneous
    treatment effects with Bayesian post-estimation (scmBayesPost), and write
    tidy CSV tables with formatted HTML/LaTeX twins. A directory-based lock
    protocol lets several machines on one shared filesystem work on the same
    run. Phase 0 provides the timeline, spec, registry, lock/job layers and a
    synthetic panel generator; model stages follow in later phases.
